
Start the incremental migration of the existing
PropertiesManager to the new hierarchical
configuration system.

Focus only on the existing getProperty(String)
read operation.

Requirements:

1. Keep the PropertiesManager class unchanged
   as a public API.

2. Preserve all existing public method names,
   signatures, modifiers and return types.

3. When a valid configuration context is active,
   resolve the property through the existing
   configuration engine and current snapshot.

4. Reuse the existing context, resolver and
   configuration infrastructure.

5. Do not create a second configuration store,
   coordinator or global mutable singleton.

6. Preserve legacy behavior for executions
   that do not use the new lifecycle integration.

7. Never silently fall back to ROOT or stale
   thread-local values when a scoped context
   is expected.

8. Do not attempt to infer an ITestResult inside
   a zero-argument or key-only API.

9. Do not change setProperty, setProperties,
   getProperties or other methods yet.

10. Do not modify production listeners.

11. Keep the core independent of TestNG.

12. If the existing architecture cannot safely
    locate the configuration engine from the
    active context, identify the exact missing
    dependency before implementing a workaround.

Add tests covering:
- ROOT, SUITE, TEST, CLASS and INVOCATION reads.
- Scope inheritance and source precedence.
- Parallel invocation isolation.
- Legacy behavior without the new adapter.
- Missing active-context behavior.

Run focused tests and the affected module.

